# Top-level dependencies (source of truth for the hash-pinned lock file).
# Regenerate the lock with network access, ONE lock for every platform:
#   python -m pip install uv
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 -o requirements.lock
# --universal matters: a lock made on Windows with pip-compile leaves out Linux-only
# packages (e.g. uvloop, needed by chromadb's server extras), and the Linux install
# then fails with "all requirements must have their versions pinned with ==".
# Install in production with:
#   pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.lock
-r requirements.txt
